<title>USA: Interactive Flight signs $1.6 mln pact.</title>
<headline>Interactive Flight signs $1.6 mln pact.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interactive Flight Technologies Inc said Friday it signed a letter of intent with PetrolAir to install an in-flight entertainment system for $1.6 million.</p>
<p>The company said it expects to begin installation next year. The system will offer passengers in-flight entertainment options including casino style gambling, digitized movies on-demand, video games and interactive shopping.</p>
</text>
